  "worked_solution": "Trigonometric functions are continuous at all points in their respective domains.\n\nThe function $\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x$ is continuous over the entire interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}],$ but the function $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ is not defined at $x=\\pi .$ \n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ consists of the union of the intervals $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ),$ and $(\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}],$ namely\n\n$$\n[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi )\\cup (\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
